window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["ansible"]=[{"id":"ansible-f0001","card":"q-ansible-001-what-ansible-is-and-how-it-differs-from","sec":"ansible-s002","q":"What is Ansible, and why is it used?","a":"<p>Ansible automates configuration management, application deployment and ad-hoc tasks. It is agentless (uses SSH), simple (YAML-based), cuts manual errors and keeps systems consistent.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0002","card":"q-ansible-001-what-ansible-is-and-how-it-differs-from","sec":"ansible-s002","q":"How does Ansible differ from Puppet or Chef?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Ansible</strong>: agentless (SSH), push-based, YAML playbooks.</li>\n  <li><strong>Puppet/Chef</strong>: agent-based, pull-based, use a DSL or Ruby.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ansible is simpler and lighter, with no master-agent complexity.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0003","card":"q-ansible-002-architecture","sec":"ansible-s003","q":"What is the architecture of Ansible?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Control node</strong>: runs Ansible.</li>\n  <li><strong>Managed nodes</strong>: the targets; need SSH and Python.</li>\n  <li><strong>Inventory</strong>: lists hosts.</li>\n  <li><strong>Modules</strong>: the task executors.</li>\n  <li><strong>Playbooks</strong>: YAML workflows.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0004","card":"q-ansible-003-playbooks-roles-modules","sec":"ansible-s004","q":"What is an Ansible Playbook?","a":"<p>A YAML file defining tasks and workflows for automation (for example install Nginx, then start it). It is the blueprint for what happens on which hosts.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0005","card":"q-ansible-003-playbooks-roles-modules","sec":"ansible-s004","q":"Difference between Playbooks and Roles?","a":"<p>A playbook is a full automation script. A role is a modular, reusable chunk (tasks, vars, templates) that playbooks call for structure.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0006","card":"q-ansible-003-playbooks-roles-modules","sec":"ansible-s004","q":"What are Ansible Modules? How do they work?","a":"<p>Modules are scripts that perform tasks (file operations, package installs). Ansible ships them to the hosts over SSH, executes them, and cleans up. They are idempotent by design.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0007","card":"q-ansible-003-playbooks-roles-modules","sec":"ansible-s004","q":"What is an Inventory file and what is its purpose?","a":"<p>It lists the hosts (IPs, names, groups) Ansible targets, static or dynamic, for example <code>[webservers] web1</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0008","card":"q-ansible-004-connection-and-transport","sec":"ansible-s005","q":"How does Ansible connect to remote hosts?","a":"<p>Via SSH by default. The control node authenticates (keys or passwords), sends modules, runs them with Python, and removes them. WinRM is used for Windows.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0009","card":"q-ansible-004-connection-and-transport","sec":"ansible-s005","q":"Default transport mechanism?","a":"<p>SSH. It is secure, agentless, and relies on the existing SSH setup on the hosts.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0010","card":"q-ansible-005-ansible-vs-ansible-playbook-idempotency","sec":"ansible-s006","q":"Difference between <code>ansible</code> and <code>ansible-playbook</code>?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>ansible</code>: ad-hoc, single tasks (<code>ansible all -m ping</code>).</li>\n  <li><code>ansible-playbook</code>: runs full YAML playbooks for structured automation.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0011","card":"q-ansible-005-ansible-vs-ansible-playbook-idempotency","sec":"ansible-s006","q":"What is idempotency and why is it key?","a":"<p>Tasks only change a system if needed, for example skipping an install when the package is already present. That keeps results consistent, avoids redundant actions, and makes runs reliable.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0012","card":"q-ansible-006-prerequisites-and-installation","sec":"ansible-s007","q":"Prerequisites for installing Ansible?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Control node</strong>: Linux or macOS, Python 3.8+, SSH client.</li>\n  <li><strong>Managed nodes</strong>: SSH server, Python 2.6+/3.5+, network access. No agents.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0013","card":"q-ansible-006-prerequisites-and-installation","sec":"ansible-s007","q":"How to install Ansible on Linux?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sudo apt update\nsudo apt install ansible\n# or\npip install ansible\nansible --version</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0014","card":"q-ansible-006-prerequisites-and-installation","sec":"ansible-s007","q":"How to upgrade Ansible?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sudo apt install --only-upgrade ansible\npip install --upgrade ansible</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0015","card":"q-ansible-007-the-ansible-cfg-file","sec":"ansible-s008","q":"Purpose of the <code>ansible.cfg</code> file?","a":"<p>It customizes Ansible: inventory path, SSH options, escalation settings. It avoids repeating CLI flags and keeps runs consistent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Ini</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>[defaults]\ninventory = ./inventory\nremote_user = ansible\nprivate_key_file = ~/.ssh/id_rsa\nhost_key_checking = False\nretry_files_enabled = False\nlog_path = ./ansible.log\n\n[privilege_escalation]\nbecome = True\nbecome_method = sudo\nbecome_user = root\nbecome_ask_pass = False</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0016","card":"q-ansible-009-ad-hoc-commands","sec":"ansible-s010","q":"Run a single task without a playbook?","a":"<p>Use <code>ansible</code> with <code>-m</code> (module) and <code>-a</code> (args):</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible all -m ping\nansible webservers -m command -a &quot;uptime&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0017","card":"q-ansible-009-ad-hoc-commands","sec":"ansible-s010","q":"What is <code>ansible-doc</code>?","a":"<p>It shows module documentation, usage and parameters:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-doc apt</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0018","card":"q-ansible-010-static-and-dynamic-inventories","sec":"ansible-s011","q":"Types of inventories?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Static</strong>: a manual host list (file).</li>\n  <li><strong>Dynamic</strong>: a script or plugin pulls hosts (for example from AWS).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Static suits small setups; dynamic scales.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0019","card":"q-ansible-010-static-and-dynamic-inventories","sec":"ansible-s011","q":"Dynamic vs static inventory?","a":"<p>Dynamic auto-fetches hosts from sources such as AWS via scripts or plugins. Static is a fixed, manual file. Dynamic scales, static is simple.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0020","card":"q-ansible-011-defining-and-grouping-hosts","sec":"ansible-s012","q":"Define a static inventory / group hosts?","a":"<p>INI:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Ini</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>[webservers]\nweb1.example.com\n[dbservers]\ndb1.example.com</code></pre></div>\n<p>YAML:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>all:\n  children:\n    webservers:\n      hosts:\n        web1.example.com:</code></pre></div>\n<p>Use with <code>-i hosts</code>, and target groups in playbooks (<code>hosts: webservers</code>).</p>\n<p>A fuller INI inventory with two hosts per group:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Ini</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>[webservers]\nweb1.example.com ansible_host=192.168.1.10\nweb2.example.com ansible_host=192.168.1.11\n[dbservers]\ndb1.example.com ansible_host=192.168.1.20\ndb2.example.com ansible_host=192.168.1.21</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0021","card":"q-ansible-012-inventory-variables-and-ansible-host","sec":"ansible-s013","q":"Specify variables in an inventory?","a":"<p>INI:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Ini</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>web1.example.com ansible_user=admin\n[webservers:vars]\nhttp_port=80</code></pre></div>\n<p>YAML:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>webservers:\n  hosts:\n    web1.example.com:\n      ansible_user: admin\n  vars:\n    http_port: 80</code></pre></div>\n<p>These are used in tasks and templates.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0022","card":"q-ansible-012-inventory-variables-and-ansible-host","sec":"ansible-s013","q":"Purpose of the <code>ansible_host</code> variable?","a":"<p>It sets the real IP or hostname for an alias. With the line below, targeting <code>web1</code> connects to <code>192.168.1.10</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Ini</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>web1 ansible_host=192.168.1.10</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0023","card":"q-ansible-013-multiple-environments-and-the-l-flag","sec":"ansible-s014","q":"Inventory for multiple environments (dev, prod)?","a":"<p>Use a single file with environment groups, or separate files such as <code>dev_hosts</code> and <code>prod_hosts</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Ini</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>[dev_webservers]\ndev-web1\n[prod_webservers]\nprod-web1</code></pre></div>\n<p>Run: <code>ansible-playbook -i hosts -l dev</code>.</p>\n<p>The <code>-l</code> (or <code>--limit</code>) flag limits execution to the hosts matching the pattern, here <code>dev</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0024","card":"q-ansible-014-testing-connectivity-i-flag-and-cloud-in","sec":"ansible-s015","q":"Test connectivity to inventory hosts?","a":"<p><code>ansible all -m ping</code> checks SSH and Python on all hosts. Add <code>-i</code> for a custom inventory.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0025","card":"q-ansible-014-testing-connectivity-i-flag-and-cloud-in","sec":"ansible-s015","q":"What is the <code>-i</code> flag?","a":"<p>It specifies the inventory file or script and overrides the default <code>/etc/ansible/hosts</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible -i my_hosts all -m ping</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0026","card":"q-ansible-014-testing-connectivity-i-flag-and-cloud-in","sec":"ansible-s015","q":"Use a cloud provider for dynamic inventory (AWS)?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>plugin: aws_ec2\nregions:\n  - us-east-1</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible -i aws_ec2.yml all -m ping</code></pre></div>\n<p>It fetches hosts dynamically.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0027","card":"q-ansible-015-yaml-and-basic-playbook-structure","sec":"ansible-s016","q":"What is YAML, and why does Ansible use it?","a":"<p>A human-readable format that relies on indentation. It makes playbooks simple and clear for defining automation.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0028","card":"q-ansible-015-yaml-and-basic-playbook-structure","sec":"ansible-s016","q":"Structure a basic Playbook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>---\n- name: Install Nginx\n  hosts: webservers\n  tasks:\n    - name: Install\n      apt:\n        name: nginx\n        state: present\n    - name: Start\n      service:\n        name: nginx\n        state: started</code></pre></div>\n<p>It targets hosts and lists tasks.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0029","card":"q-ansible-015-yaml-and-basic-playbook-structure","sec":"ansible-s016","q":"Key Playbook components?","a":"<p><code>hosts</code> (targets), <code>tasks</code> (actions), <code>vars</code> (variables), <code>name</code> (labels), <code>become</code> (sudo), <code>handlers</code> (triggered tasks).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0030","card":"q-ansible-016-verbose-output-and-variables","sec":"ansible-s017","q":"Run a Playbook with verbose output?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook playbook.yml -v</code></pre></div>\n<p>Add <code>-vv</code>, <code>-vvv</code>, <code>-vvvv</code> for more detail.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0031","card":"q-ansible-016-verbose-output-and-variables","sec":"ansible-s017","q":"Include variables in a Playbook?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Inline:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vars:\n  package_name: nginx</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n  <li>File:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vars_files:\n  - vars/main.yml</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n  <li>CLI:</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook -e &quot;package_name=nginx&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0032","card":"q-ansible-016-verbose-output-and-variables","sec":"ansible-s017","q":"<code>vars</code> vs <code>vars_files</code>?","a":"<p><code>vars</code> holds inline variables in the playbook (local). <code>vars_files</code> loads an external YAML file (modular).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0033","card":"q-ansible-017-conditionals-become-and-loops","sec":"ansible-s018","q":"Use conditionals (<code>when</code>)?","a":"<p>The task runs only if the condition is true.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install on Ubuntu\n  apt:\n    name: nginx\n    state: present\n  when: ansible_os_family == &quot;Debian&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0034","card":"q-ansible-017-conditionals-become-and-loops","sec":"ansible-s018","q":"Purpose of <code>become</code>?","a":"<p>It escalates privileges (sudo).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install Nginx\n  apt:\n    name: nginx\n    state: present\n  become: yes</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0035","card":"q-ansible-017-conditionals-become-and-loops","sec":"ansible-s018","q":"Loop over a list?","a":"<p>The task runs once per item.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install packages\n  apt:\n    name: &quot;{{ item }}&quot;\n    state: present\n  loop:\n    - nginx\n    - git</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0036","card":"q-ansible-018-handlers","sec":"ansible-s019","q":"What is the <code>handlers</code> section?","a":"<p>Handlers are tasks triggered by <code>notify</code>; they run only when the notifying task reports a change.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Copy config\n  copy:\n    src: nginx.conf\n    dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\n  notify: Restart Nginx\nhandlers:\n  - name: Restart Nginx\n    service:\n      name: nginx\n      state: restarted</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0037","card":"q-ansible-019-debugging-register-and-errors","sec":"ansible-s020","q":"Debug Playbook execution?","a":"<p>Use <code>-v</code>, add a debug task, or use <code>--step</code> and <code>--check</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- debug:\n    msg: &quot;Value: {{ my_var }}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0038","card":"q-ansible-019-debugging-register-and-errors","sec":"ansible-s020","q":"What is <code>register</code>?","a":"<p>It captures task output into a variable.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Check package\n  command: dpkg -l nginx\n  register: result\n- debug:\n    msg: &quot;Installed&quot;\n  when: result.rc == 0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0039","card":"q-ansible-019-debugging-register-and-errors","sec":"ansible-s020","q":"Handle errors with <code>ignore_errors</code>?","a":"<p>The play continues on failure.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Remove file\n  file:\n    path: /tmp/test.txt\n    state: absent\n  ignore_errors: yes</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0040","card":"q-ansible-020-include-vs-import","sec":"ansible-s021","q":"Difference: <code>include</code> vs <code>import</code>?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>include</code> (for example <code>include_tasks: setup.yml</code>): runtime, dynamic.</li>\n  <li><code>import</code> (for example <code>import_tasks: setup.yml</code>): parse-time, static.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th><code>include_tasks</code></th><th><code>import_tasks</code></th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Processing time</td><td>At runtime (dynamic)</td><td>At parse-time (static)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Flexibility</td><td>Can use runtime variables and conditions</td><td>Variables must be known at parse-time</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Performance</td><td>Slightly slower (runtime evaluation)</td><td>Faster (pre-loaded during parsing)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Use case</td><td>Conditional or dynamic task inclusion</td><td>Static, predictable task inclusion</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Debugging</td><td>Harder (resolved at runtime)</td><td>Easier (resolved before execution)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0041","card":"q-ansible-024-tags","sec":"ansible-s025","q":"Use tags in a Playbook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install\n  apt:\n    name: nginx\n    state: present\n  tags:\n    - install</code></pre></div>\n<p>Run:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook --tags &quot;install&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0042","card":"q-ansible-025-common-modules-and-command-vs-shell","sec":"ansible-s026","q":"Commonly used modules?","a":"<p><code>command</code>, <code>shell</code>, <code>file</code>, <code>copy</code>, <code>yum</code>/<code>apt</code>, <code>service</code>, <code>template</code>, <code>user</code>, <code>setup</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0043","card":"q-ansible-025-common-modules-and-command-vs-shell","sec":"ansible-s026","q":"Use the <code>command</code> module? Limitations?","a":"<p>It has no shell features (pipes, redirects); use <code>shell</code> for those.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Run command\n  command: uptime</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0044","card":"q-ansible-025-common-modules-and-command-vs-shell","sec":"ansible-s026","q":"<code>shell</code> vs <code>command</code>?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>command</code>: direct, no shell (for example <code>uptime</code>).</li>\n  <li><code>shell</code>: runs through a shell, supports pipes (for example <code>ls &gt; file</code>).</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0045","card":"q-ansible-026-file-packages-copy-and-service","sec":"ansible-s027","q":"Use the <code>file</code> module?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- file:\n    path: /opt/app\n    state: directory\n    mode: &#x27;0755&#x27;\n- file:\n    path: /tmp/test.txt\n    state: absent</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0046","card":"q-ansible-026-file-packages-copy-and-service","sec":"ansible-s027","q":"Install a package with <code>yum</code>/<code>apt</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- yum:\n    name: httpd\n    state: present\n- apt:\n    name: nginx\n    state: present</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0047","card":"q-ansible-026-file-packages-copy-and-service","sec":"ansible-s027","q":"What is the <code>copy</code> module for?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- copy:\n    src: config.conf\n    dest: /etc/app/config.conf\n    mode: &#x27;0644&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0048","card":"q-ansible-026-file-packages-copy-and-service","sec":"ansible-s027","q":"Manage services with <code>service</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- service:\n    name: nginx\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0049","card":"q-ansible-027-template-vs-copy","sec":"ansible-s028","q":"How is <code>template</code> different from <code>copy</code>?","a":"<p><code>template</code> renders a Jinja2 file with variables, loops and conditionals; <code>copy</code> transfers a static file as-is.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- template:\n    src: httpd.conf.j2\n    dest: /etc/httpd/httpd.conf</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th><code>copy</code></th><th><code>template</code></th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>File content</td><td>Static, copied as-is</td><td>Dynamic, processed as Jinja2</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Use case</td><td>Scripts, binaries, static config</td><td>Configs that vary by host or environment</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Source file</td><td>Any file</td><td>Jinja2 template (<code>.j2</code> by convention)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Flexibility</td><td>No dynamic content</td><td>Variable substitution, loops, conditionals</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<p>Variables can be used in the <code>src</code> and <code>dest</code> paths of both modules, but only <code>template</code> processes variables inside the file content.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0050","card":"q-ansible-029-lineinfile-and-user","sec":"ansible-s030","q":"What is <code>lineinfile</code> for?","a":"<p>It edits a single line, useful for config tweaks.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- lineinfile:\n    path: /etc/ssh/sshd_config\n    regexp: &#x27;^PermitRootLogin&#x27;\n    line: &#x27;PermitRootLogin no&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0051","card":"q-ansible-029-lineinfile-and-user","sec":"ansible-s030","q":"Manage users with <code>user</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- user:\n    name: appuser\n    password: &quot;{{ &#x27;pass&#x27; | password_hash(&#x27;sha512&#x27;) }}&quot;\n    state: present</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0052","card":"q-ansible-030-fetch","sec":"ansible-s031","q":"Fetch files with <code>fetch</code>?","a":"<p><code>fetch</code> pulls files from the remote host to the control node, the opposite of <code>copy</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- fetch:\n    src: /var/log/app.log\n    dest: /local/logs/{{ inventory_hostname }}.log\n    flat: yes</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>src</code> is the file on the remote host.</li>\n  <li><code>dest</code> is the path on the control node; <code>{{ inventory_hostname }}</code> keeps files from different hosts from overwriting each other (<code>/local/logs/dev-web1.log</code>, <code>/local/logs/prod-web1.log</code>).</li>\n  <li><code>flat: yes</code> saves directly to <code>dest</code>. Without it, the remote path is mirrored (for example <code>/local/logs/dev-web1/var/log/app.log</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Typical uses are collecting logs for debugging or auditing, backing up configuration files, and centralizing files from many hosts.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Fetch logs from remote hosts\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n    - name: Fetch app.log from remote host\n      ansible.builtin.fetch:\n        src: /var/log/app.log\n        dest: /local/logs/{{ inventory_hostname }}.log\n        flat: yes</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0053","card":"q-ansible-031-setup-and-custom-modules","sec":"ansible-s032","q":"What is the <code>setup</code> module?","a":"<p>It gathers facts. It runs automatically unless <code>gather_facts: no</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- setup:</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0054","card":"q-ansible-031-setup-and-custom-modules","sec":"ansible-s032","q":"Write a custom module?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from ansible.module_utils.basic import AnsibleModule\ndef main():\n    module = AnsibleModule(argument_spec=dict(name=dict(type=&#x27;str&#x27;, required=True)))\n    module.exit_json(changed=True, msg=f&quot;Hello, {module.params[&#x27;name&#x27;]}&quot;)\nif __name__ == &#x27;__main__&#x27;:\n    main()</code></pre></div>\n<p>Use it in a playbook:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- my_custom_module:\n    name: &quot;world&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0055","card":"q-ansible-032-facts-and-variables","sec":"ansible-s033","q":"What are Ansible Facts?","a":"<p>Host data (OS, IP) collected automatically by the <code>setup</code> module at the start of a play.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0056","card":"q-ansible-032-facts-and-variables","sec":"ansible-s033","q":"Access facts in a Playbook?","a":"<p>Use <code>ansible_facts['key']</code> or dot notation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- debug:\n    msg: &quot;Host: {{ ansible_hostname }}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0057","card":"q-ansible-032-facts-and-variables","sec":"ansible-s033","q":"Facts vs variables?","a":"<p>Facts are dynamic and come from the hosts. Variables are static and user-defined.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0058","card":"q-ansible-033-defining-variables-and-precedence","sec":"ansible-s034","q":"Define variables at different levels?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Inventory: <code>web1 ansible_user=admin</code></li>\n  <li>Playbook: <code>vars:</code> with <code>app: nginx</code></li>\n  <li>Role: <code>defaults/main.yml</code></li>\n  <li>CLI: <code>-e \"app=nginx\"</code></li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0059","card":"q-ansible-033-defining-variables-and-precedence","sec":"ansible-s034","q":"Variable precedence?","a":"<p>Low to high: role defaults, inventory, playbook vars, CLI <code>-e</code>. The higher one wins.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0060","card":"q-ansible-033-defining-variables-and-precedence","sec":"ansible-s034","q":"Override a variable during execution?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook playbook.yml -e &quot;app_version=2.0&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0061","card":"q-ansible-034-jinja2-filters-set-fact-and-group-vars","sec":"ansible-s035","q":"Jinja2 filters with variables?","a":"<p>Examples: <code>{{ var | upper }}</code>, <code>{{ list | join(',') }}</code>, <code>{{ var | default('n/a') }}</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0062","card":"q-ansible-034-jinja2-filters-set-fact-and-group-vars","sec":"ansible-s035","q":"Use <code>set_fact</code> for custom facts?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- set_fact:\n    custom_ver: &quot;1.5&quot;\n- debug:\n    msg: &quot;{{ custom_ver }}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0063","card":"q-ansible-034-jinja2-filters-set-fact-and-group-vars","sec":"ansible-s035","q":"What is <code>group_vars</code>?","a":"<p>A directory for group variables, one file per group:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># group_vars/webservers.yml\nhttp_port: 80</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0064","card":"q-ansible-035-encrypting-variables-with-vault","sec":"ansible-s036","q":"What is Ansible Vault?","a":"<p>It encrypts secrets (passwords, API keys) in files so they can be stored safely, even in version control.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0065","card":"q-ansible-035-encrypting-variables-with-vault","sec":"ansible-s036","q":"Encrypt variables with Vault?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-vault create secrets.yml</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db_pass: secret</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook --ask-vault-pass</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>ansible-vault create</code> prompts for a vault password and opens an editor. The saved file is AES256-encrypted on disk (it starts with <code>$ANSIBLE_VAULT;1.1;AES256</code>).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0066","card":"q-ansible-037-vault-commands-and-passwords","sec":"ansible-s038","q":"Edit a vault-encrypted file?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-vault edit secrets.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0067","card":"q-ansible-037-vault-commands-and-passwords","sec":"ansible-s038","q":"Use a vault variable in a playbook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vars_files:\n  - secrets.yml\ntasks:\n  - debug:\n      msg: &quot;{{ my_secret }}&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<p>Run with <code>--ask-vault-pass</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0068","card":"q-ansible-037-vault-commands-and-passwords","sec":"ansible-s038","q":"Single-file vs multi-file encryption?","a":"<p>Single: one file, one password. Multi: multiple files with separate passwords or IDs.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0069","card":"q-ansible-037-vault-commands-and-passwords","sec":"ansible-s038","q":"Specify the vault password?","a":"<p>Use <code>--ask-vault-pass</code> or <code>--vault-password-file pass.txt</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0070","card":"q-ansible-038-multiple-vault-passwords-with-vault-ids","sec":"ansible-s039","q":"Manage multiple vault passwords?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-vault encrypt secrets.yml --vault-id dev@prompt\nansible-playbook --vault-id dev@dev_pass.txt</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>--vault-id dev@prompt</code>: <code>dev</code> is a user-defined label and <code>prompt</code> means the password is typed in.</li>\n  <li><code>--vault-id dev@dev_pass.txt</code>: Ansible reads the password for the <code>dev</code> label from <code>dev_pass.txt</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Different environments can use different IDs (<code>dev@prompt</code>, <code>prod@prod_pass.txt</code>), and several <code>--vault-id</code> flags can be passed in one run. A password file holds the plaintext password, so restrict it (<code>chmod 600 dev_pass.txt</code>) or use a secrets manager.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0071","card":"q-ansible-039-what-roles-are-and-how-to-create-one","sec":"ansible-s040","q":"What are Roles? Why useful?","a":"<p>Modular bundles of tasks and variables (for example web setup). They are reusable, organized, and reduce playbook clutter.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0072","card":"q-ansible-039-what-roles-are-and-how-to-create-one","sec":"ansible-s040","q":"Create a role?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-galaxy init my_role</code></pre></div>\n<p>It creates <code>tasks/</code>, <code>vars/</code> and the other standard directories.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0073","card":"q-ansible-039-what-roles-are-and-how-to-create-one","sec":"ansible-s040","q":"Role directory structure?","a":"<p><code>tasks/</code>, <code>defaults/</code>, <code>vars/</code>, <code>handlers/</code>, <code>templates/</code>, <code>files/</code>, <code>meta/</code>, <code>tests/</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0074","card":"q-ansible-039-what-roles-are-and-how-to-create-one","sec":"ansible-s040","q":"Call a role in a playbook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- hosts: webservers\n  roles:\n    - my_role</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0075","card":"q-ansible-040-tasks-vs-defaults","sec":"ansible-s041","q":"Tasks vs defaults in a role?","a":"<p><code>tasks/</code> holds the actions (install, configure). <code>defaults/</code> holds fallback variables with the lowest precedence, so any other source overrides them.</p>\n<p><code>roles/my_role/tasks/main.yml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install nginx\n  ansible.builtin.package:\n    name: nginx\n    state: present\n\n- name: Ensure nginx is running\n  ansible.builtin.service:\n    name: nginx\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>roles/my_role/defaults/main.yml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>port: 80\nwebserver_user: www-data</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0076","card":"q-ansible-041-passing-variables-to-a-role","sec":"ansible-s042","q":"Pass variables to a role?","a":"<p>Variables passed in the playbook override the role defaults, so the same role serves different environments (for example port 8080 for dev and 443 for prod).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- hosts: webservers\n  roles:\n    - role: my_role\n      vars:\n        port: 8080</code></pre></div>\n<p>If <code>port</code> is not passed, the role falls back to the default <code>port: 80</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0077","card":"q-ansible-042-reusing-roles-across-playbooks","sec":"ansible-s043","q":"Reuse roles across playbooks?","a":"<p>Store them in <code>roles/</code> and call them with <code>roles:</code> or <code>include_role</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible_project/\n├── playbooks/\n│   └── deploy.yml\n├── roles/\n│   └── my_role/\n│       ├── tasks/main.yml\n│       ├── defaults/main.yml\n│       └── templates/nginx.conf.j2\n└── inventory</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>roles:</code> applies the role at play level, before the play's tasks. <code>include_role</code> applies it as a task, giving control over when it runs (inside a loop or conditionally).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Apply my_role dynamically\n  hosts: webservers\n  tasks:\n    - name: Include my_role with custom port\n      ansible.builtin.include_role:\n        name: my_role\n      vars:\n        port: 8080</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0078","card":"q-ansible-045-meta-galaxy-and-role-debugging","sec":"ansible-s046","q":"Purpose of the <code>meta</code> directory?","a":"<p><code>meta/main.yml</code> defines role dependencies and info:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dependencies:\n  - role: common</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0079","card":"q-ansible-045-meta-galaxy-and-role-debugging","sec":"ansible-s046","q":"Install roles from Galaxy?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-galaxy install geerlingguy.nginx</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- roles:\n    - geerlingguy.nginx</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0080","card":"q-ansible-045-meta-galaxy-and-role-debugging","sec":"ansible-s046","q":"Debug role issues?","a":"<p>Use <code>-v</code>, <code>--check</code> and tags, and add a debug task:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- debug:\n    var: my_var</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0081","card":"q-ansible-046-tower-awx-ssh-keys-check-mode-limit","sec":"ansible-s047","q":"What is Ansible Tower/AWX?","a":"<p>A GUI, API and workflow layer over Ansible. Core Ansible is CLI only; Tower (commercial) and AWX (open source) add scheduling and RBAC. AWX can be installed with Docker or Kubernetes, then used to create projects, inventories and job templates (for example schedule a playbook daily).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0082","card":"q-ansible-046-tower-awx-ssh-keys-check-mode-limit","sec":"ansible-s047","q":"Configure Ansible with SSH keys?","a":"<p>Generate a key (<code>ssh-keygen</code>), copy it to hosts (<code>ssh-copy-id</code>), and set it in the inventory or <code>ansible.cfg</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0083","card":"q-ansible-046-tower-awx-ssh-keys-check-mode-limit","sec":"ansible-s047","q":"Purpose of the <code>--check</code> flag?","a":"<p>A dry run: it simulates the playbook without making changes.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0084","card":"q-ansible-046-tower-awx-ssh-keys-check-mode-limit","sec":"ansible-s047","q":"Limit a playbook to specific hosts?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook playbook.yml --limit webservers</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0085","card":"q-ansible-047-delegate-to","sec":"ansible-s048","q":"What is <code>delegate_to</code>?","a":"<p>It runs a task on another host.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- command: script.sh\n  delegate_to: localhost</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0086","card":"q-ansible-048-parallel-execution-and-forks","sec":"ansible-s049","q":"How does parallel execution work?","a":"<p>Forks (default 5) run tasks across hosts concurrently, while tasks on each single host run sequentially. With 10 hosts and the default, Ansible does 5 hosts, then the next 5.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0087","card":"q-ansible-048-parallel-execution-and-forks","sec":"ansible-s049","q":"What are <code>forks</code>?","a":"<p>The number of parallel processes. Higher forks (for example 20) speed up large runs but strain the control node (CPU, memory, SSH connections). Set it with <code>-f</code> or in <code>ansible.cfg</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0088","card":"q-ansible-050-optimizing-ansible-for-scale","sec":"ansible-s051","q":"Optimize Ansible for scale?","a":"<p>More forks, pipelining, dynamic inventory, fact caching, and Tower/AWX.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0089","card":"q-ansible-054-strategies","sec":"ansible-s055","q":"What is <code>strategy</code>?","a":"<p>The task execution mode:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>linear</code> (default): waits for all hosts to finish a task before the next one.</li>\n  <li><code>free</code>: each host proceeds independently, so faster hosts do not wait.</li>\n  <li><code>debug</code>: interactive, for troubleshooting.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Test linear strategy\n  hosts: webservers\n  strategy: linear\n  tasks:\n    - name: Task 1 - Simulate variable delay\n      ansible.builtin.command: &quot;sleep {{ sleep_time }}&quot;\n      vars:\n        sleep_time: &quot;{{ 2 if inventory_hostname in [&#x27;host1&#x27;, &#x27;host2&#x27;] else 5 }}&quot;\n    - name: Task 2 - Output\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg: &quot;Task 2 on {{ inventory_hostname }}&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<p>Setting <code>strategy: free</code> or <code>strategy: debug</code> on a play works the same way. With <code>linear</code>, everyone waits for the 5-second hosts; with <code>free</code>, <code>host1</code> and <code>host2</code> move to Task 2 after 2 seconds.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0090","card":"q-ansible-055-docker-jenkins-and-collections","sec":"ansible-s056","q":"Use Ansible with Docker?","a":"<p>It needs the Docker SDK.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- docker_container:\n    name: nginx\n    image: nginx:latest\n    state: started</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0091","card":"q-ansible-055-docker-jenkins-and-collections","sec":"ansible-s056","q":"Integrate Ansible with CI/CD (Jenkins)?","a":"<p>Use the Jenkins plugin and credentials.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Groovy</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansiblePlaybook playbook: &#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;, inventory: &#x27;hosts&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0092","card":"q-ansible-055-docker-jenkins-and-collections","sec":"ansible-s056","q":"What are Collections?","a":"<p>Bundles of modules and roles, versus standalone roles.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-galaxy collection install</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0093","card":"q-ansible-055-docker-jenkins-and-collections","sec":"ansible-s056","q":"Troubleshoot a failed task?","a":"<p>Use <code>-v</code> and <code>--check</code>, add debug tasks, and test connectivity with <code>ping</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0094","card":"q-ansible-066-two-tasks-modify-the-same-file-delegatio","sec":"ansible-s067","q":"Two tasks modify the same file?","a":"<p>The last task wins unless you use <code>lineinfile</code> or <code>blockinfile</code> to append. Design for idempotency.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0095","card":"q-ansible-066-two-tasks-modify-the-same-file-delegatio","sec":"ansible-s067","q":"Run a task once, on a delegated host?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- command: echo &quot;once&quot;\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: true</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0096","card":"q-ansible-067-network-devices","sec":"ansible-s068","q":"Can Ansible manage network devices?","a":"<p>Yes, with modules like <code>ios_config</code>. It uses <code>network_cli</code> over SSH or NETCONF.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- cisco.ios.ios_config:\n    lines:\n      - hostname NEW_ROUTER</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0097","card":"q-ansible-068-limitations-and-secrets","sec":"ansible-s069","q":"Limitations of Ansible?","a":"<p>It is slower (SSH), has no real-time operation, is less expressive than Ruby/DSL tools, and has weaker network support.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0098","card":"q-ansible-068-limitations-and-secrets","sec":"ansible-s069","q":"Secrets beyond Vault?","a":"<p>Use HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, or lookups:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- debug:\n    msg: &quot;{{ lookup(&#x27;hashi_vault&#x27;, &#x27;secret/my-key&#x27;) }}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0099","card":"q-ansible-069-changed-vs-ok-races-unreachable-hosts","sec":"ansible-s070","q":"Difference between <code>changed</code> and <code>ok</code>?","a":"<p><code>changed</code> means the system was modified. <code>ok</code> means no change was needed.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0100","card":"q-ansible-069-changed-vs-ok-races-unreachable-hosts","sec":"ansible-s070","q":"Handle race conditions?","a":"<p>Execution is sequential per host; use <code>serial</code> or <code>run_once</code> for shared resources.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0101","card":"q-ansible-069-changed-vs-ok-races-unreachable-hosts","sec":"ansible-s070","q":"What happens with an unreachable host in the inventory?","a":"<p>It is marked <code>UNREACHABLE</code> and the playbook continues, unless <code>any_errors_fatal</code> is set.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0102","card":"q-ansible-070-scale-and-ci-cd-failures","sec":"ansible-s071","q":"Scale Ansible for thousands of hosts?","a":"<p>More forks, dynamic inventory, Tower, fact caching, and optimized playbooks.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0103","card":"q-ansible-070-scale-and-ci-cd-failures","sec":"ansible-s071","q":"A playbook fails in CI/CD but works locally?","a":"<p>Check version mismatch, credentials, inventory, and network differences. Standardize the environment and test with <code>-v</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0104","card":"q-ansible-071-ad-hoc-pings-copy-and-uptime","sec":"ansible-s072","q":"Ad-hoc command to ping all hosts?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible all -m ping</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0105","card":"q-ansible-071-ad-hoc-pings-copy-and-uptime","sec":"ansible-s072","q":"Copy <code>config.conf</code> to <code>/etc/app/</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible all -m copy -a &quot;src=config.conf dest=/etc/app/config.conf owner=root mode=0644&quot; --become</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0106","card":"q-ansible-071-ad-hoc-pings-copy-and-uptime","sec":"ansible-s072","q":"Check uptime of <code>dbservers</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible dbservers -m command -a &quot;uptime&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0107","card":"q-ansible-071-ad-hoc-pings-copy-and-uptime","sec":"ansible-s072","q":"Update the package cache on Ubuntu?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible all -m apt -a &quot;update_cache=yes&quot; --become -l ubuntu_hosts</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0108","card":"q-ansible-072-install-httpd-and-manage-nginx","sec":"ansible-s073","q":"Playbook to install <code>httpd</code> on <code>webservers</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install httpd\n  hosts: webservers\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Install httpd\n    ansible.builtin.yum: { name: httpd, state: present }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook install_httpd.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0109","card":"q-ansible-072-install-httpd-and-manage-nginx","sec":"ansible-s073","q":"Playbook to start and enable <code>nginx</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Manage nginx\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Install nginx\n    ansible.builtin.package: { name: nginx, state: present }\n  - name: Start nginx\n    ansible.builtin.service: { name: nginx, state: started, enabled: yes }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook nginx_service.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0110","card":"q-ansible-073-rolling-restarts-and-reboots","sec":"ansible-s074","q":"Restart <code>webservers</code> sequentially?","a":"<p><code>serial: 1</code> processes one host at a time.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Restart webservers\n  hosts: webservers\n  become: yes\n  serial: 1\n  tasks:\n  - name: Restart\n    ansible.builtin.reboot:</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook reboot_webservers.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0111","card":"q-ansible-073-rolling-restarts-and-reboots","sec":"ansible-s074","q":"Reboot hosts and wait for them to return?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible all -m reboot -a &quot;reboot_timeout=300&quot; --become</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0112","card":"q-ansible-074-users-facts-and-shell-output","sec":"ansible-s075","q":"Playbook for user <code>devops</code> with UID 2000?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Create devops user\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Create user\n    ansible.builtin.user: { name: devops, uid: 2000, state: present }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook create_user.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0113","card":"q-ansible-074-users-facts-and-shell-output","sec":"ansible-s075","q":"Set a fact based on the OS distribution?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Set OS fact\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n  - name: Set fact\n    ansible.builtin.set_fact: { os_dist: &quot;{{ ansible_facts[&#x27;distribution&#x27;] }}&quot; }\n  - name: Debug\n    ansible.builtin.debug: { var: os_dist }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0114","card":"q-ansible-074-users-facts-and-shell-output","sec":"ansible-s075","q":"Run a shell command and register the output?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Run shell\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n  - name: Get disk space\n    ansible.builtin.shell: &quot;df -h /&quot;\n    register: disk_space\n  - name: Debug\n    ansible.builtin.debug: { var: disk_space.stdout }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook shell_command.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0115","card":"q-ansible-075-templates-stat-and-handlers","sec":"ansible-s076","q":"Deploy the template <code>app.conf.j2</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Deploy template\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Deploy\n    ansible.builtin.template: { src: app.conf.j2, dest: /etc/app.conf, owner: root, mode: &quot;0644&quot; }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook deploy_template.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0116","card":"q-ansible-075-templates-stat-and-handlers","sec":"ansible-s076","q":"Check if a file exists and print a debug message?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Check file\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n  - name: Check file\n    ansible.builtin.stat: { path: /etc/app.conf }\n    register: file_status\n  - name: Debug\n    ansible.builtin.debug: { msg: &quot;File exists&quot; }\n    when: file_status.stat.exists</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook check_file.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0117","card":"q-ansible-075-templates-stat-and-handlers","sec":"ansible-s076","q":"Playbook with a handler to restart <code>httpd</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Manage httpd\n  hosts: webservers\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Deploy config\n    ansible.builtin.copy: { src: httpd.conf, dest: /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf, owner: root }\n    notify: Restart httpd\n  handlers:\n  - name: Restart httpd\n    ansible.builtin.service: { name: httpd, state: restarted }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook httpd_config.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0118","card":"q-ansible-076-loops-conditionals-and-cron","sec":"ansible-s077","q":"Loop over a package list?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install packages\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  vars: { packages: [nginx, git, curl] }\n  tasks:\n  - name: Install\n    ansible.builtin.package: { name: &quot;{{ item }}&quot;, state: present }\n    loop: &quot;{{ packages }}&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook install_packages.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0119","card":"q-ansible-076-loops-conditionals-and-cron","sec":"ansible-s077","q":"Run a task only on Debian?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Debian task\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n  - name: Update cache\n    ansible.builtin.apt: { update_cache: yes }\n    when: ansible_os_family == &quot;Debian&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook debian_task.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0120","card":"q-ansible-076-loops-conditionals-and-cron","sec":"ansible-s077","q":"Playbook for a daily cron job at midnight?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Setup cron\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Create cron\n    ansible.builtin.cron: { name: &quot;Daily backup&quot;, minute: &quot;0&quot;, hour: &quot;0&quot;, job: &quot;/usr/local/bin/backup.sh&quot; }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook cron_backup.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0121","card":"q-ansible-077-gather-facts-delegate-and-remove-directo","sec":"ansible-s078","q":"Gather facts and save them to a file?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible all -m setup -a &quot;gather_subset=all&quot; --tree /tmp/facts</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0122","card":"q-ansible-077-gather-facts-delegate-and-remove-directo","sec":"ansible-s078","q":"Delegate a task to localhost?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Delegate to localhost\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n  - name: Run locally\n    ansible.builtin.command: &quot;echo {{ inventory_hostname }} &gt;&gt; /tmp/host_list&quot;\n    delegate_to: localhost</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook delegate_task.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0123","card":"q-ansible-077-gather-facts-delegate-and-remove-directo","sec":"ansible-s078","q":"Playbook to remove <code>/tmp/old_data</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Remove directory\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Remove\n    ansible.builtin.file: { path: /tmp/old_data, state: absent }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook remove_dir.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0124","card":"q-ansible-078-tags-lineinfile-and-verbose-troubleshoot","sec":"ansible-s079","q":"Run a playbook with the <code>deploy</code> tag?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook playbook.yml --tags &quot;deploy&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0125","card":"q-ansible-078-tags-lineinfile-and-verbose-troubleshoot","sec":"ansible-s079","q":"Ensure a line in <code>/etc/hosts</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Update hosts\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Add line\n    ansible.builtin.lineinfile: { path: /etc/hosts, line: &quot;192.168.1.100 app.example.com&quot; }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook update_hosts.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0126","card":"q-ansible-078-tags-lineinfile-and-verbose-troubleshoot","sec":"ansible-s079","q":"Troubleshoot a playbook with verbose output?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook playbook.yml -v</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0127","card":"q-ansible-079-apply-a-manifest-and-verify-the-pod","sec":"ansible-s080","q":"Ansible to apply a K8s manifest and verify?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Apply K8s\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Apply\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl apply -f pod.yaml\n  - name: Verify\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl get pod nginx-pod -o jsonpath=&#x27;{.status.phase}&#x27;\n    register: pod_status\n  - name: Fail if not running\n    ansible.builtin.fail: { msg: &quot;Pod not Running&quot; }\n    when: pod_status.stdout != &quot;Running&quot;</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>pod.yaml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata: { name: nginx-pod }\nspec: { containers: [{ name: nginx, image: &quot;nginx:latest&quot; }] }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0128","card":"q-ansible-079-apply-a-manifest-and-verify-the-pod","sec":"ansible-s080","q":"Troubleshoot an Ansible-deployed pod that is not running?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kubectl get pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl describe pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl logs &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\nkubectl get pod &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt; -o yaml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0129","card":"q-ansible-080-install-kubectl-and-check-the-cluster","sec":"ansible-s081","q":"Ansible to install <code>kubectl</code> and check the cluster?","a":"<p>The <code>creates</code> argument keeps the install step idempotent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Install kubectl\n  hosts: all\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Install\n    ansible.builtin.shell: |\n      curl -LO &quot;https://dl.k8s.io/release/$(curl -L -s https://dl.k8s.io/release/stable.txt)/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl&quot;\n      chmod +x kubectl &amp;&amp; mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/\n    args: { creates: /usr/local/bin/kubectl }\n  - name: Check cluster\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl cluster-info\n    register: cluster_info\n  - name: Debug\n    ansible.builtin.debug: { var: cluster_info.stdout }</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ansible-playbook install_kubectl.yml</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0130","card":"q-ansible-081-update-a-configmap-and-restart-pods","sec":"ansible-s082","q":"Ansible to update a ConfigMap and restart pods?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Update ConfigMap\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Apply\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl apply -f configmap.yaml\n  - name: Restart\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl rollout restart deployment web-app -n default</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>configmap.yaml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata: { name: app-config }\ndata: { env: &quot;production&quot; }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0131","card":"q-ansible-082-check-pod-logs-and-fail-on-errors","sec":"ansible-s083","q":"Ansible task to check pod logs and fail on errors?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Check logs\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Get logs\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl logs &lt;pod-name&gt; -n &lt;namespace&gt;\n    register: pod_logs\n  - name: Fail on error\n    ansible.builtin.fail: { msg: &quot;Errors in logs&quot; }\n    when: &quot;&#x27;error&#x27; in pod_logs.stdout | lower&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0132","card":"q-ansible-083-deploy-a-service-and-expose-it-externall","sec":"ansible-s084","q":"Ansible to deploy a K8s Service and expose it externally?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Deploy service\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n  - name: Apply\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl apply -f service.yaml\n  - name: Expose\n    ansible.builtin.command: kubectl expose service web-service --type=LoadBalancer --port=80 --name=web-lb -n default</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>service.yaml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>apiVersion: v1\nkind: Service\nmetadata: { name: web-service }\nspec:\n  selector: { app: web-app }\n  ports: [{ port: 80, targetPort: 8080 }]\n  type: ClusterIP</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0133","card":"q-ansible-084-run-an-ansible-playbook-from-github-acti","sec":"ansible-s085","q":"GitHub Actions to run an Ansible playbook on push?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Run Ansible\non: { push: { branches: [main] } }\njobs:\n  ansible:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - run: sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install -y ansible\n    - run: ansible-playbook playbook.yml -i inventory.ini</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>playbook.yml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Test\n  hosts: all\n  tasks:\n  - name: Ping\n    ansible.builtin.ping:</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0134","card":"q-ansible-085-configure-a-k8s-node-with-ansible-from-g","sec":"ansible-s086","q":"GitHub Actions with Ansible to configure a K8s node and verify?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Configure Node\non: { push: { branches: [main] } }\njobs:\n  configure:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - run: sudo apt update &amp;&amp; sudo apt install -y ansible\n    - run: ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini configure_node.yml\n    - uses: azure/setup-kubectl@v3\n    - run: echo &quot;${{ secrets.KUBECONFIG }}&quot; &gt; $HOME/.kube/config\n    - run: kubectl get nodes</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>configure_node.yml</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>- name: Configure node\n  hosts: k8s_nodes\n  become: yes\n  tasks:\n  - name: Install kubeadm\n    ansible.builtin.package: { name: kubeadm, state: present }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0135","card":"q-ansible-086-infrastructure-as-code-and-ansible-vs-te","sec":"ansible-s087","q":"What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC), and how do Terraform and Ansible support it?","a":"<p>IaC manages and provisions infrastructure through machine-readable definition files instead of manual processes, giving automation, consistency and version control.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Terraform</strong>: a declarative tool using HCL; supports many cloud providers and tracks resources in a state file.</li>\n  <li><strong>Ansible</strong>: a procedural tool using YAML playbooks; agentless over SSH, strong at configuration management and application deployment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Terraform focuses on provisioning and Ansible on configuration.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0136","card":"q-ansible-086-infrastructure-as-code-and-ansible-vs-te","sec":"ansible-s087","q":"Key differences between Ansible and Terraform when managing AWS resources?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Approach</strong>: Terraform is declarative (desired state); Ansible is procedural (steps to reach a state).</li>\n  <li><strong>Focus</strong>: Terraform provisions infrastructure (creating EC2 instances); Ansible configures it (installing software on instances).</li>\n  <li><strong>State</strong>: Terraform keeps a state file; Ansible is stateless.</li>\n  <li><strong>Python integration</strong>: Terraform uses <code>python-terraform</code> or <code>subprocess</code>; Ansible uses the <code>ansible</code> Python API, <code>ansible-runner</code> or custom modules.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0137","card":"q-ansible-087-how-ansible-uses-python","sec":"ansible-s088","q":"How does Ansible use Python under the hood, and why is Python a good fit?","a":"<p>Ansible is written in Python and uses it for:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Module execution</strong>: most modules are Python scripts executed on the target hosts.</li>\n  <li><strong>API integration</strong>: the <code>ansible</code> Python package allows programmatic playbook execution.</li>\n  <li><strong>Extensibility</strong>: custom modules can be written in Python.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Python fits because of its simplicity, extensive libraries, cross-platform compatibility, and ability to handle complex automation logic.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0138","card":"q-ansible-087-how-ansible-uses-python","sec":"ansible-s088","q":"How does Python integrate with Ansible for resource management?","a":"<p>Python scripts can use the <code>ansible</code> module to run playbooks programmatically, or create custom modules.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0139","card":"q-ansible-087-how-ansible-uses-python","sec":"ansible-s088","q":"How do you ensure idempotency with Ansible?","a":"<p>Use <code>state</code> parameters (for example <code>state=present</code>) and check conditions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0140","card":"q-ansible-088-custom-ansible-modules-in-python","sec":"ansible-s089","q":"What is the role of Python in writing custom Ansible modules?","a":"<p>Custom modules are Python scripts that extend Ansible. They accept arguments as JSON input, return JSON output with results or errors, and use the <code>AnsibleModule</code> class for argument parsing and error handling.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0141","card":"q-ansible-088-custom-ansible-modules-in-python","sec":"ansible-s089","q":"How do you create a custom Ansible module in Python?","a":"<p>Use <code>AnsibleModule</code> to handle input parameters and output, and place the module in a <code>library/</code> directory in the Ansible project (for example <code>library/custom_module.py</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>#!/usr/bin/python\nfrom ansible.module_utils.basic import AnsibleModule\n\ndef main():\n    module_args = dict(\n        name=dict(type=&#x27;str&#x27;, required=True),\n        state=dict(type=&#x27;str&#x27;, default=&#x27;present&#x27;, choices=[&#x27;present&#x27;, &#x27;absent&#x27;])\n    )\n\n    module = AnsibleModule(\n        argument_spec=module_args,\n        supports_check_mode=True\n    )\n\n    name = module.params[&#x27;name&#x27;]\n    state = module.params[&#x27;state&#x27;]\n\n    result = dict(changed=False, message=&quot;&quot;)\n\n    if state == &#x27;present&#x27;:\n        result[&#x27;changed&#x27;] = True\n        result[&#x27;message&#x27;] = f&quot;Resource {name} created&quot;\n    else:\n        result[&#x27;changed&#x27;] = True\n        result[&#x27;message&#x27;] = f&quot;Resource {name} deleted&quot;\n\n    module.exit_json(**result)\n\nif __name__ == &#x27;__main__&#x27;:\n    main()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0142","card":"q-ansible-089-the-ansible-python-api","sec":"ansible-s090","q":"What is the purpose of the <code>ansible</code> Python API, and how is it used to run playbooks programmatically?","a":"<p>It lets Python scripts run playbooks and tasks, integrate Ansible with other tools, and customize execution parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from ansible import context\nfrom ansible.cli import CLI\nfrom ansible.module_utils.common.collections import ImmutableDict\nfrom ansible.executor.playbook_executor import PlaybookExecutor\n\ncontext.CLIARGS = ImmutableDict(tags={}, listtags=False, listtasks=False, listhosts=False,\n                               syntax=False, connection=&#x27;smart&#x27;, module_path=None,\n                               forks=100, private_key_file=None, ssh_common_args=None,\n                               ssh_extra_args=None, sftp_extra_args=None, scp_extra_args=None,\n                               become=None, become_method=None, become_user=None, verbosity=0,\n                               check=False, diff=False)\n\nplaybook_path = &#x27;playbook.yml&#x27;\nexecutor = PlaybookExecutor(playbooks=[playbook_path], inventory=None,\n                            variable_manager=None, loader=None, passwords=None)\nexecutor.run()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0143","card":"q-ansible-090-ad-hoc-command-through-the-python-api","sec":"ansible-s091","q":"Write a Python script to execute an ad-hoc Ansible command using the <code>ansible</code> Python API.","a":"<p>The <code>ansible</code> Python API is internal and less stable than <code>ansible-runner</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from ansible import context\nfrom ansible.cli import CLI\nfrom ansible.module_utils.common.collections import ImmutableDict\nfrom ansible.executor.task_queue_manager import TaskQueueManager\nfrom ansible.inventory.manager import InventoryManager\nfrom ansible.parsing.dataloader import DataLoader\nfrom ansible.playbook.play import Play\nfrom ansible.vars.manager import VariableManager\n\n# Setup context\nloader = DataLoader()\ncontext.CLIARGS = ImmutableDict(tags={}, listtags=False, listtasks=False, listhosts=False,\n                               syntax=False, connection=&#x27;smart&#x27;, module_path=None, forks=10,\n                               remote_user=&#x27;user&#x27;, private_key_file=None, ssh_common_args=None,\n                               ssh_extra_args=None, sftp_extra_args=None, scp_extra_args=None,\n                               become=False, become_method=&#x27;sudo&#x27;, become_user=&#x27;root&#x27;, verbosity=0,\n                               check=False, diff=False)\n\n# Initialize inventory and variables\ninventory = InventoryManager(loader=loader, sources=[&#x27;/path/to/inventory&#x27;])\nvariable_manager = VariableManager(loader=loader, inventory=inventory)\n\n# Define ad-hoc command\nplay_source = dict(\n    name=&quot;Ad-hoc command&quot;,\n    hosts=&quot;all&quot;,\n    gather_facts=&quot;no&quot;,\n    tasks=[\n        dict(action=dict(module=&quot;command&quot;, args=dict(cmd=&quot;uptime&quot;)))\n    ]\n)\n\n# Create play\nplay = Play().load(play_source, variable_manager=variable_manager, loader=loader)\n\n# Run the play\ntqm = None\ntry:\n    tqm = TaskQueueManager(\n        inventory=inventory,\n        variable_manager=variable_manager,\n        loader=loader,\n        passwords=dict(),\n    )\n    result = tqm.run(play)\nfinally:\n    if tqm is not None:\n        tqm.cleanup()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0144","card":"q-ansible-091-run-a-playbook-with-ansible-runner","sec":"ansible-s092","q":"How do you run an Ansible playbook programmatically using <code>ansible-runner</code>?","a":"<p>Install it with <code>pip install ansible-runner</code> and use the <code>run</code> function.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import ansible_runner\n\n# Run an Ansible playbook\nr = ansible_runner.run(\n    private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n    playbook=&#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;,\n    inventory=&#x27;/path/to/inventory&#x27;\n)\n\n# Check the result\nif r.rc == 0:\n    print(&quot;Playbook executed successfully&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(f&quot;Playbook failed with status: {r.rc}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0145","card":"q-ansible-092-parse-playbook-output-and-log-results","sec":"ansible-s093","q":"How do you parse Ansible playbook output and extract results?","a":"<p>Run the playbook with <code>ansible-runner</code> and parse the JSON events under the <code>job_events</code> folder of the artifacts directory in the <code>private_data_dir</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import ansible_runner\nimport json\nimport os\n\n# Run playbook\nr = ansible_runner.run(\n    private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n    playbook=&#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;\n)\n\n# Parse results\nartifacts_dir = os.path.join(r.config.artifact_dir, &#x27;job_events&#x27;)\nfor event_file in os.listdir(artifacts_dir):\n    with open(os.path.join(artifacts_dir, event_file)) as f:\n        event_data = json.load(f)\n        if &#x27;event_data&#x27; in event_data and &#x27;task&#x27; in event_data[&#x27;event_data&#x27;]:\n            task = event_data[&#x27;event_data&#x27;][&#x27;task&#x27;]\n            result = event_data[&#x27;event_data&#x27;].get(&#x27;res&#x27;, {})\n            print(f&quot;Task: {task}, Result: {result}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0146","card":"q-ansible-092-parse-playbook-output-and-log-results","sec":"ansible-s093","q":"Run a playbook and log the results to a file?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import ansible_runner\nimport json\n\n# Run playbook\nr = ansible_runner.run(\n    private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n    playbook=&#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;\n)\n\n# Log results\nwith open(&#x27;ansible_log.json&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n    json.dump({\n        &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;success&#x27; if r.rc == 0 else &#x27;failed&#x27;,\n        &#x27;return_code&#x27;: r.rc,\n        &#x27;stats&#x27;: r.stats\n    }, f, indent=2)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0147","card":"q-ansible-093-generate-a-dynamic-inventory","sec":"ansible-s094","q":"Write a Python script to dynamically generate an Ansible inventory file.","a":"<p>Write the host and group information to a file in YAML or INI format.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import yaml\n\n# Define inventory data\ninventory = {\n    &#x27;webservers&#x27;: {\n        &#x27;hosts&#x27;: [&#x27;web1.example.com&#x27;, &#x27;web2.example.com&#x27;],\n        &#x27;vars&#x27;: {\n            &#x27;http_port&#x27;: 80\n        }\n    },\n    &#x27;dbservers&#x27;: {\n        &#x27;hosts&#x27;: [&#x27;db1.example.com&#x27;]\n    }\n}\n\n# Write to inventory file\nwith open(&#x27;inventory.yml&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n    yaml.dump(inventory, f)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0148","card":"q-ansible-094-handle-playbook-failures-and-pass-variab","sec":"ansible-s095","q":"How do you handle Ansible playbook failures in a Python script?","a":"<p>Check the return code (<code>rc</code>), parse the output or logs from <code>ansible-runner</code>, use try-except, and add retry logic if needed.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import ansible_runner\n\ntry:\n    r = ansible_runner.run(\n        private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n        playbook=&#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;\n    )\n    if r.rc != 0:\n        print(f&quot;Playbook failed with exit code: {r.rc}&quot;)\n        # Retry logic\n        max_attempts = 3\n        for attempt in range(max_attempts):\n            retry_r = ansible_runner.run(\n                private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n                playbook=&#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;\n            )\n            if retry_r.rc == 0:\n                print(&quot;Retry successful&quot;)\n                break\n            print(f&quot;Retry {attempt + 1} failed&quot;)\n    else:\n        print(&quot;Playbook succeeded&quot;)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error running playbook: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0149","card":"q-ansible-094-handle-playbook-failures-and-pass-variab","sec":"ansible-s095","q":"How do you pass variables to a playbook from a Python script?","a":"<p>Use the <code>extravars</code> parameter of <code>ansible-runner</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import ansible_runner\n\n# Define extra variables\nextra_vars = {\n    &#x27;http_port&#x27;: 8080,\n    &#x27;app_version&#x27;: &#x27;1.2.3&#x27;\n}\n\n# Run playbook with extra variables\nr = ansible_runner.run(\n    private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n    playbook=&#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;,\n    extravars=extra_vars\n)\n\nprint(f&quot;Playbook executed with status: {r.rc}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0150","card":"q-ansible-095-validate-syntax-before-running","sec":"ansible-s096","q":"How do you validate playbook syntax from Python before execution?","a":"<p>Run <code>ansible-playbook --syntax-check</code> through <code>ansible-runner</code> and confirm there are no errors.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import ansible_runner\n\n# Run syntax check\nr = ansible_runner.run(\n    private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n    playbook=&#x27;deploy.yml&#x27;,\n    cmdline=&#x27;--syntax-check&#x27;\n)\n\nif r.rc == 0:\n    print(&quot;Syntax check passed&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(f&quot;Syntax check failed: {r.rc}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0151","card":"q-ansible-096-integrate-ansible-with-aws-ec2-through-b","sec":"ansible-s097","q":"How can Python integrate Ansible with AWS services (EC2 provisioning)?","a":"<p>Use <code>boto3</code> to read AWS state and pass the result to Ansible as inventory or variables. Here running EC2 instances become an inventory, then a playbook is run against it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport yaml\n\n# Initialize boto3 client\nec2 = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n\n# Get EC2 instances\nresponse = ec2.describe_instances()\n\n# Create inventory\ninventory = {&#x27;webservers&#x27;: {&#x27;hosts&#x27;: []}}\nfor reservation in response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;]:\n    for instance in reservation[&#x27;Instances&#x27;]:\n        if instance[&#x27;State&#x27;][&#x27;Name&#x27;] == &#x27;running&#x27;:\n            inventory[&#x27;webservers&#x27;][&#x27;hosts&#x27;].append(instance[&#x27;PublicDnsName&#x27;])\n\n# Write inventory\nwith open(&#x27;inventory.yml&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n    yaml.dump(inventory, f)\n\n# Run Ansible playbook\nimport ansible_runner\nansible_runner.run(\n    private_data_dir=&#x27;/path/to/ansible/project&#x27;,\n    playbook=&#x27;configure_web.yml&#x27;,\n    inventory=&#x27;inventory.yml&#x27;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0152","card":"q-ansible-097-validate-aws-credentials-before-a-playbo","sec":"ansible-s098","q":"Scenario: the playbook fails provisioning EC2 because of incorrect credentials. How would Python validate credentials first?","a":"<p>Make a simple API call such as <code>sts.get_caller_identity</code> with <code>boto3</code>, and run the playbook only if it succeeds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport subprocess\nimport botocore\n\ndef validate_aws_credentials():\n    try:\n        sts = boto3.client(&quot;sts&quot;)\n        sts.get_caller_identity()\n        print(&quot;AWS credentials are valid&quot;)\n        return True\n    except botocore.exceptions.ClientError as e:\n        print(f&quot;Invalid AWS credentials: {e}&quot;)\n        return False\n\ndef run_ansible_playbook(playbook_path):\n    if validate_aws_credentials():\n        subprocess.run([&quot;ansible-playbook&quot;, playbook_path], check=True)\n        print(&quot;Ansible playbook executed successfully&quot;)\n    else:\n        print(&quot;Aborting playbook execution due to invalid credentials&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nrun_ansible_playbook(&quot;provision_ec2.yml&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0153","card":"q-ansible-098-speed-up-a-slow-playbook-across-many-ins","sec":"ansible-s099","q":"Scenario: a playbook takes too long across many AWS instances. How would Python optimize it?","a":"<p>Parallelize with <code>concurrent.futures</code> or group instances into batches, and validate instance availability with <code>boto3</code> first.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport subprocess\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\n\ndef run_ansible_playbook(instances, playbook_path):\n    ec2 = boto3.client(&quot;ec2&quot;)\n    response = ec2.describe_instances(InstanceIds=instances)\n    valid_instances = [i[&quot;InstanceId&quot;] for r in response[&quot;Reservations&quot;] for i in r[&quot;Instances&quot;] if i[&quot;State&quot;][&quot;Name&quot;] == &quot;running&quot;]\n\n    def execute_playbook(instance_id):\n        subprocess.run([&quot;ansible-playbook&quot;, playbook_path, &quot;-i&quot;, f&quot;{instance_id},&quot;], check=True)\n        print(f&quot;Playbook executed on {instance_id}&quot;)\n\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=5) as executor:\n        executor.map(execute_playbook, valid_instances)\n\n# Example usage\nrun_ansible_playbook([&quot;i-1234567890abcdef0&quot;, &quot;i-0987654321fedcba0&quot;], &quot;deploy.yml&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0154","card":"q-ansible-099-automate-rds-backups-with-python-and-ans","sec":"ansible-s100","q":"Scenario: automate the backup of an AWS RDS database using Python and Ansible. How would you design it?","a":"<p>Use <code>boto3</code> to create the snapshot and wait until it is available, and an Ansible playbook to orchestrate the run.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport time\n\ndef create_rds_snapshot(db_instance_id, snapshot_id):\n    rds = boto3.client(&quot;rds&quot;)\n    rds.create_db_snapshot(DBInstanceIdentifier=db_instance_id, DBSnapshotIdentifier=snapshot_id)\n    print(f&quot;Creating snapshot {snapshot_id}&quot;)\n\n    while True:\n        response = rds.describe_db_snapshots(DBSnapshotIdentifier=snapshot_id)\n        status = response[&quot;DBSnapshots&quot;][0][&quot;Status&quot;]\n        if status == &quot;available&quot;:\n            print(&quot;Snapshot created successfully&quot;)\n            break\n        time.sleep(30)\n\n# Example usage\ncreate_rds_snapshot(&quot;my-db-instance&quot;, &quot;my-snapshot-2023&quot;)</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># Ansible playbook: backup_rds.yml\n- name: Backup RDS\n  hosts: localhost\n  tasks:\n    - name: Run Python script to create RDS snapshot\n      command: python create_rds_snapshot.py\n      environment:\n        AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID: &quot;{{ lookup(&#x27;env&#x27;, &#x27;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&#x27;) }}&quot;\n        AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY: &quot;{{ lookup(&#x27;env&#x27;, &#x27;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&#x27;) }}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"ansible-f0155","card":"q-ansible-100-ansible-failing-on-kubernetes-nodes-with","sec":"ansible-s101","q":"Scenario: a playbook fails on certain Kubernetes nodes due to network issues. How would Python diagnose and resolve it?","a":"<p>Use the <code>kubernetes</code> client to check node status, <code>boto3</code> to verify network configuration (VPC, security groups), then restart or replace the problematic nodes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from kubernetes import client, config\nimport boto3\n\ndef diagnose_k8s_nodes(namespace):\n    config.load_kube_config()\n    v1 = client.CoreV1Api()\n\n    nodes = v1.list_node()\n    for node in nodes.items:\n        for condition in node.status.conditions:\n            if condition.type == &quot;NetworkUnavailable&quot; and condition.status == &quot;True&quot;:\n                print(f&quot;Node {node.metadata.name} has network issues&quot;)\n                # Check AWS network configuration\n                ec2 = boto3.client(&quot;ec2&quot;)\n                response = ec2.describe_instances(Filters=[{&quot;Name&quot;: &quot;private-dns-name&quot;, &quot;Values&quot;: [node.metadata.name]}])\n                instance_id = response[&quot;Reservations&quot;][0][&quot;Instances&quot;][0][&quot;InstanceId&quot;]\n                ec2.reboot_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n                print(f&quot;Rebooted node {node.metadata.name}&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\ndiagnose_k8s_nodes(&quot;default&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false}];
